# Assignments module (P8) — demo requests (VS / Rider / VS Code REST Client).
#
# One-time local setup (Development) is the same as users.http. Submitted files go to App_Data/files next to the host
# (Storage:RootPath); that folder is git-ignored.
# Prerequisites: scheduling.http + lifecycle.http (active term, a subject the professor teaches, a registered student).

@host = http://localhost:5080
@adminToken = paste-the-admin-token-here
@professorToken = paste-the-teaching-professors-token-here
@studentToken = paste-a-registered-students-token-here
@subjectId = paste-a-subject-id-here
@assignmentId = paste-the-id-from-the-create-here
@submissionId = paste-the-id-from-the-submit-here

### Professor (teaching the subject): create → 201 (whole subject, or one group via subjectGroupId; defaults pdf,docx,zip and 10 MB)
POST {{host}}/api/assignments
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": "{{subjectId}}",
  "title": "Assignment 2 — Shortest paths",
  "instructions": "Implement Dijkstra and submit the report.",
  "dueAt": "2026-12-01T21:59:00Z",
  "maxGrade": 20,
  "allowedExtensions": "pdf,zip",
  "maxFileMb": 10
}

### Teacher / registered student / admin: this term's assignments (status=open|closed, paged)
GET {{host}}/api/assignments?subjectId={{subjectId}}&status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### One assignment (invisible → 404)
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Teacher: edit (subject and group never change; after the first submission only texts change and the deadline can only move later)
PUT {{host}}/api/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": "{{subjectId}}",
  "title": "Assignment 2 — Shortest paths (updated)",
  "instructions": "Implement Dijkstra and Bellman-Ford.",
  "dueAt": "2026-12-03T21:59:00Z",
  "maxGrade": 20,
  "allowedExtensions": "pdf,zip",
  "maxFileMb": 10
}

### Student: submit once before the deadline (multipart) → 201 with the receipt (SUB-yyyy-000001); a second try → 409
POST {{host}}/api/assignments/{{assignmentId}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=NIMI

--NIMI
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="report.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

%PDF-1.7 demo
--NIMI--

### Teacher: the assignment's submissions (status=submitted|approved|rejected, paged)
GET {{host}}/api/assignments/{{assignmentId}}/submissions?status=submitted
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Teacher or the submitting student: download the file
GET {{host}}/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/file
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}

### Teacher: approve with a grade (≤ max), once; the student is notified
PUT {{host}}/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/review
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "approve", "grade": 18, "feedback": "Clean implementation." }

### Teacher: or reject with a reason
# PUT {{host}}/api/submissions/{{submissionId}}/review
# Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "decision": "reject", "rejectionReason": "Wrong file — please contact me." }

### Student: my submissions with receipt, status, grade and feedback
GET {{host}}/api/submissions/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{studentToken}}

### Teacher: delete → 204 (only while it has no submissions; otherwise 409)
DELETE {{host}}/api/assignments/{{assignmentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{professorToken}}
